-- title:
--   Function field of a base change by a field extension
-- statement:
--   Let $K \subseteq K'$ be fields with $K'$ a $K$-algebra, let $X$ be a scheme with a morphism $\pi_X : X \to \operatorname{Spec} K$, and assume both $X$ and the pullback $X' := X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} K} \operatorname{Spec} K'$ (formed along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $K \to K'$) are integral schemes. Let $F$ be a field and a $K$-algebra together with a ring isomorphism $e_F : F \cong \mathcal{O}_{X,\eta}$ onto the function field of $X$ (the stalk at the generic point) such that, for every $a \in K$, $e_F(a)$ is the germ at the generic point of the global section obtained from $a$ via $\pi_X$ on global sections, i.e. $e_F \circ (\text{structure map of } F) =$ `baseToFunctionField` $\pi_X$. Let $F'$ be a field and a $K'$-algebra, and $\mathrm{to}' : F \to F'$ a ring homomorphism compatible with the structure maps, so that the image of $a \in K$ in $F'$ through $F$ agrees with its image through $K'$. Assume the subfield of $F'$ generated by the union of the images of $K'$ and of $F$ is all of $F'$, and that $\mathrm{to}'$ preserves linear independence in the sense that for each finite subset $s \subseteq F$ which is $K$-linearly independent, the family $(\mathrm{to}'(x))_{x \in s}$ is $K'$-linearly independent. Then there is a ring isomorphism $e_{F'}$ from $F'$ onto the function field of $X'$ which (i) sends each $z \in K'$, viewed in $F'$, to the germ at the generic point of $X'$ of the global section coming from $z$ via the second projection $X' \to \operatorname{Spec} K'$, and (ii) for every open $U \subseteq X$ with $U$ and its preimage in $X'$ under the first projection both non-empty, and every $t \in \Gamma(X,U)$, sends $\mathrm{to}'(e_F^{-1}(\text{germ of } t))$ to the germ in the function field of $X'$ of the pullback of $t$ along the first projection over the preimage of $U$.
--
--   This identifies the function field of a constant field extension $X \times_K \operatorname{Spec} K'$ of an integral $K$-scheme, for an arbitrary extension $K'/K$, with a compositum $F' = K' \cdot F$ in which $K'$ and $F$ are linearly disjoint over $K$, compatibly with germs of sections. It is used in the construction of a complex curve model with a prescribed identification of places in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, where the extension taken is $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \hookrightarrow \mathbb{C}$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_exists_ringEquiv_functionField_pullback_of_closure_eq_top_of_linearIndependent_of_isIntegral_pullback.lean

